WEBVTT

NOTE Original complete video/audio are preserved.
Source speech alignment and confirmed corrections are recorded privately.

1
00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.230 position:50% align:center size:90%
Another issue I would like to address in
this testimonial about virtues

2
00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.930 position:50% align:center size:90%
is how hard it is for people who have been
through prison to get past

3
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.090 position:50% align:center size:90%
what happened, the mistake they made.

4
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:18.370 position:50% align:center size:90%
Even after going through prison, being
deprived of their

5
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:23.230 position:50% align:center size:90%
freedom and serving their sentence, they
remain paralyzed by guilt.

6
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:28.290 position:50% align:center size:90%
It is as if they could no longer
reintegrate into society,

7
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.410 position:50% align:center size:90%
thinking: “No one will accept me anymore

8
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:36.370 position:50% align:center size:90%
because I committed a crime.” That makes
the second chance

9
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:40.810 position:50% align:center size:90%
people deserve to start over much harder.
I believe that by working on virtues,

10
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.790 position:50% align:center size:90%
especially acceptance—accepting the
mistake you made,

11
00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.370 position:50% align:center size:90%
which you cannot go back and
change—accepting it is the best

12
00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:55.390 position:50% align:center size:90%
way to face that situation. And
forgiveness: forgive yourself.

13
00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:56.940 position:50% align:center size:90%
What do I mean by that?

14
00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.470 position:50% align:center size:90%
We are all human and liable to make
mistakes. In other words,

15
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:06.130 position:50% align:center size:90%
you will be paying—you have already paid
for the mistake you made. So

16
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:11.650 position:50% align:center size:90%
work on acceptance and self-forgiveness.
That certainly

17
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:17.590 position:50% align:center size:90%
makes dignified reintegration possible, an
evolution that truly

18
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:18.770 position:50% align:center size:90%
has to do with virtues.
